From: PlayThing builder <builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] SurfaceFlinger: screenshots with a primary display orientation

The Car Thing panel is portrait (480 x 800) and SF_PRIMARY_DISPLAY_ORIENTATION
is 90. captureScreen() takes the display scissor as the crop, but the scissor
is in panel coordinates, and renderScreenImplLocked() turns a given crop from
display coordinates to panel coordinates again. The crop becomes
(-320, 0, 480, 480): screencap and the window manager's rotation animation show
the left 480 columns of the screen, stretched, above a black band. With a
primary display orientation, the scissor is not used: the crop is then the
whole panel (the default in renderScreenImplLocked), and updateDimensions()
gives the size. Without a primary display orientation, nothing changes.

---
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
@@ -4767,7 +4767,12 @@
     if (CC_UNLIKELY(device == 0)) return BAD_VALUE;
 
     const Rect& dispScissor = device->getScissor();
-    if (!dispScissor.isEmpty()) {
+    // PlayThing: with a primary display orientation (a panel mounted turned), the scissor is in
+    // panel coordinates, but renderScreenImplLocked turns a given crop from display coordinates
+    // to panel coordinates again. The screenshot (screencap, the rotation animation) then shows
+    // a stretched part of the screen. So without the scissor: the crop is then the whole panel,
+    // and updateDimensions gives the size.
+    if (!dispScissor.isEmpty() && mPrimaryDisplayOrientation == DisplayState::eOrientationDefault) {
         sourceCrop.set(dispScissor);
         // adb shell screencap will default reqWidth and reqHeight to zeros.
         if (reqWidth == 0 || reqHeight == 0) {
